  "rules": [
    "सवा N M = (N + 0.25) x M; सवा M (no N) = 1.25 x M. Example: सवा लाख = 125000, सवा सौ = 125, सवा तीन = 3.25.",
    "साढ़े N M = (N + 0.5) x M. Example: साढ़े तीन सौ = 350, साढ़े चार लाख = 450000.",
    "पौने N M = (N - 0.25) x M. Example: पौने चार = 3.75, पौने दो सौ = 175.",
    "डेढ़ M = 1.5 x M; ढाई M = 2.5 x M; आधा M = 0.5 x M. Without M they stand for 1.5, 2.5, 0.5.",
    "A Hindi number word run is evaluated left to right: values below 100 add; सौ multiplies the value so far (default 1); scales multiply and then add (दो करोड़ पचास लाख = 25000000).",
    "सौ is both a number word and a scale. Directly after सवा, डेढ़, ढाई, साढ़े, पौने or आधा it is the scale M, never the number N: सवा सौ = 1.25 x 100 = 125, not 100.25.",
    "Ordinals are never quantities. छ is accepted for 6 only as a stand-alone number word."
  ]
